{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# The ABJM su(4) alternating chain and its transfer matrices\n\n**Chain.** 2L sites, alternating A F A F … (periodic). A sites carry the 4 (ρ_A(E_ij) = e_ij, group acts by g), F sites the 4̄ (ρ_F(E_ij) = −e_ji, group acts by g^{−T}). In ABJM language: odd sites Y^A (4), even sites Y†_A (4̄) of the scalar SU(4) sector. (Paul's SoV naming calls A \"anti-fundamental\" and F \"fundamental\" — see README; only the representations matter here.)\n\nOperators: P_{ab} = Σ e_ij ⊗ e_ji (permutation of two same-type sites), K_{ab} = Σ e_ij ⊗ e_ij (projector onto the singlet Σ e_i⊗e_i of a 4⊗4̄ pair, times 4).\n\n**Minahan–Zarembo Hamiltonian** (two-loop dilatation operator in the SU(4) scalar sector):\n\nΓ = (λ²/2) Σ_{l=1}^{2L} ( 2 − 2P_{l,l+2} + P_{l,l+2}K_{l,l+1} + K_{l,l+1}P_{l,l+2} ),  λ = N/k.\n\nJ. A. Minahan, K. Zarembo, *The Bethe ansatz for superconformal Chern–Simons*, JHEP 0809:040 (2008), arXiv:0806.3951; independently D. Bak, S.-J. Rey, JHEP 0810:053 (2008), arXiv:0807.2063. Below H_MZ := Σ_l (…) (prefactor dropped).\n\n**Transfer matrices** (conventions of README / `dual-lax-t3.wb`, untwisted, inhomogeneities θ_s): T = ℒ₁⋯ℒ_{2L}, t_a = ∏_s g_s · t̄_a with\n\n- t̄₁: aux 4, ℒ_s = (u−θ_s) + h Σ e_ij ⊗ ρ_s(E_ij)  (A: u−θ+hK, F: u−θ−hP);\n- t̄₂: aux ∧² = 6, ℒ⁽²⁾_s = (u−θ̃_s) + h Σ D(e_ab) ⊗ ρ_s(E_ab), θ̃_A = θ, θ̃_F = θ+h;\n- t̄₃: aux ∧³ ≅ 4̄, ℒ̄_A = (u−θ+h) − hP, ℒ̄_F = (u−θ−3h) + hK.\n\n**Claim.** For pair-periodic inhomogeneities (θ_A on all A sites, θ_F on all F sites) the t_a commute with H_MZ **iff θ_A − θ_F = 2h** (the ABJM point), and H_MZ is the logarithmic derivative of t₁(θ_F+u) t̄₃(θ_A−h+u) at u = 0. Exact checks at L = 2 pairs, numerical at L = 3 pairs. h = 1/2 throughout.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[ee, rho, siteOpL, lax1, lax2, lax3, wedgeC, Dw, wedgeOp, mono, transfer, t1M, t2M, t3M, Pop, Kop, md, HMZ, Jtot, shiftMat, zeroQ];\nnn = 4; hh = 1/2;\nee[i_, j_] := SparseArray[{{i, j}} -> 1, {nn, nn}];\nrho[\"A\"][i_, j_] := ee[i, j]; rho[\"F\"][i_, j_] := -ee[j, i];\nid4 = IdentityMatrix[nn, SparseArray];\nsiteOpL[s_, m_, L_] := KroneckerProduct @@ Table[If[b == s, m, id4], {b, L}];\n(* the three Lax operators: entries (i,j) of the aux matrix are 4x4 site matrices *)\nlax1[ty_][v_, t_][i_, j_] := (v - t) KroneckerDelta[i, j] id4 + hh rho[ty][i, j];\nlax3[\"A\"][v_, t_][k_, l_] := (v - t + hh) KroneckerDelta[k, l] id4 - hh ee[l, k];\nlax3[\"F\"][v_, t_][k_, l_] := (v - t - 3 hh) KroneckerDelta[k, l] id4 + hh ee[k, l];\nsubs2 = Subsets[Range[nn], {2}];\nwedgeC[k_, m_, Ir_] := Which[{k, m} == Ir, 1, {m, k} == Ir, -1, True, 0];\nDw[X_] := Table[Sum[X[[k, Jc[[1]]]] wedgeC[k, Jc[[2]], Ir] + X[[k, Jc[[2]]]] wedgeC[Jc[[1]], k, Ir], {k, nn}], {Ir, subs2}, {Jc, subs2}];\nDwE = Table[Dw[Normal[ee[a, b]]], {a, nn}, {b, nn}];\nwedgeOp[ty_][iI_, iJ_] := wedgeOp[ty][iI, iJ] = Sum[DwE[[a, b, iI, iJ]] rho[ty][a, b], {a, nn}, {b, nn}];\nlax2[ty_][v_, t_][iI_, iJ_] := (v - t - If[ty == \"F\", hh, 0]) KroneckerDelta[iI, iJ] id4 + hh wedgeOp[ty][iI, iJ];\n(* monodromy and untwisted (reduced) transfer matrix, aux dimension d *)\nmono[lax_, types_, ths_, v_, d_] := Module[{L = Length[types], T},\n   T = Table[siteOpL[1, lax[types[[1]]][v, ths[[1]]][i, j], L], {i, d}, {j, d}];\n   Do[T = Table[Sum[T[[i, k]] . siteOpL[s, lax[types[[s]]][v, ths[[s]]][k, j], L], {k, d}], {i, d}, {j, d}], {s, 2, L}]; T];\ntransfer[lax_, types_, ths_, v_, d_] := With[{T = mono[lax, types, ths, v, d]}, Sum[T[[i, i]], {i, d}]];\nt1M[types_, ths_, v_] := transfer[lax1, types, ths, v, 4];\nt2M[types_, ths_, v_] := transfer[lax2, types, ths, v, 6];\nt3M[types_, ths_, v_] := transfer[lax3, types, ths, v, 4];\nzeroQ[m_] := Union[Expand[Flatten[Normal[m]]]] === {0};",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. The Minahan–Zarembo Hamiltonian\n\nH_MZ = Σ_{l=1}^{2L} (2 − 2P_{l,l+2} + P_{l,l+2}K_{l,l+1} + K_{l,l+1}P_{l,l+2}), indices mod 2L. Sanity checks at L = 2 pairs (256-dim, exact): Hermitian, su(4)-invariant ([H, J_ij] = 0 with J_ij = Σ_s ρ_s(E_ij)), invariant under translation by one pair; spectrum.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "Pop[a_, b_, L_] := Sum[siteOpL[a, ee[i, j], L] . siteOpL[b, ee[j, i], L], {i, nn}, {j, nn}];\nKop[a_, b_, L_] := Sum[siteOpL[a, ee[i, j], L] . siteOpL[b, ee[i, j], L], {i, nn}, {j, nn}];\nmd[l_, L_] := Mod[l - 1, L] + 1;\nHMZ[L_] := Sum[2 IdentityMatrix[nn^L, SparseArray] - 2 Pop[l, md[l + 2, L], L] + Pop[l, md[l + 2, L], L] . Kop[l, md[l + 1, L], L] + Kop[l, md[l + 1, L], L] . Pop[l, md[l + 2, L], L], {l, L}];\nJtot[i_, j_, types_] := Sum[siteOpL[s, rho[types[[s]]][i, j], Length[types]], {s, Length[types]}];\nshiftMat[L_] := With[{p = Flatten[Transpose[ArrayReshape[Range[nn^L], {nn^2, nn^(L - 2)}]]]}, SparseArray[Table[{k, p[[k]]} -> 1, {k, nn^L}], {nn^L, nn^L}]];\ntypes4 = {\"A\", \"F\", \"A\", \"F\"};\nH4 = HMZ[4]; S4 = shiftMat[4];\nspec4 = Tally[Eigenvalues[N[Normal[H4]]] // Chop // Round[#, 10^-8] &];\nGrid[{{\"Hermitian\", H4 == ConjugateTranspose[H4]},\n  {\"[H, J_ij] = 0 for all i, j\", And @@ Flatten[Table[zeroQ[H4 . Jtot[i, j, types4] - Jtot[i, j, types4] . H4], {i, nn}, {j, nn}]]},\n  {\"[H, S] = 0 (S = translation by one pair)\", zeroQ[H4 . S4 - S4 . H4]},\n  {\"spectrum {E, multiplicity}\", SortBy[spec4, First]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"825950\" data-output-id=\"31\" data-out-n=\"381\" data-sub-idx=\"9\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"3\" data-sub-start=\"9\" data-sub-end=\"12\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[381]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"15\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:10.8401em;vertical-align:-5.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.69em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.65em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.65em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:10.8001em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-5.15em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.65em;\"><span style=\"top:-10.66em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.85em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">Hermitian</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.46em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.85em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">[H, J_ij] = 0 for all i, j</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.26em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.85em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">[H, S] = 0 (S = translation by one pair)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4